#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-branch(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:7
msgid "git-branch - List, create, or delete branches"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git branch' [--color[=<when>] | --no-color] [--show-current]\n"
"\t[-v [--abbrev=<n> | --no-abbrev]]\n"
"\t[--column[=<options>] | --no-column] [--sort=<key>]\n"
"\t[--merged [<commit>]] [--no-merged [<commit>]]\n"
"\t[--contains [<commit>]] [--no-contains [<commit>]]\n"
"\t[--points-at <object>] [--format=<format>]\n"
"\t[(-r | --remotes) | (-a | --all)]\n"
"\t[--list] [<pattern>...]\n"
"'git branch' [--track[=(direct|inherit)] | --no-track] [-f]\n"
"\t[--recurse-submodules] <branchname> [<start-point>]\n"
"'git branch' (--set-upstream-to=<upstream> | -u <upstream>) [<branchname>]\n"
"'git branch' --unset-upstream [<branchname>]\n"
"'git branch' (-m | -M) [<oldbranch>] <newbranch>\n"
"'git branch' (-c | -C) [<oldbranch>] <newbranch>\n"
"'git branch' (-d | -D) [-r] <branchname>...\n"
"'git branch' --edit-description [<branchname>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:37
msgid ""
"If `--list` is given, or if there are no non-option arguments, existing "
"branches are listed; the current branch will be highlighted in green and "
"marked with an asterisk.  Any branches checked out in linked worktrees will "
"be highlighted in cyan and marked with a plus sign. Option `-r` causes the "
"remote-tracking branches to be listed, and option `-a` shows both local and "
"remote branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:42
msgid ""
"If a `<pattern>` is given, it is used as a shell wildcard to restrict the "
"output to matching branches. If multiple patterns are given, a branch is "
"shown if it matches any of the patterns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:46
msgid ""
"Note that when providing a `<pattern>`, you must use `--list`; otherwise the "
"command may be interpreted as branch creation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:55
msgid ""
"With `--contains`, shows only the branches that contain the named commit (in "
"other words, the branches whose tip commits are descendants of the named "
"commit), `--no-contains` inverts it. With `--merged`, only branches merged "
"into the named commit (i.e. the branches whose tip commits are reachable "
"from the named commit) will be listed.  With `--no-merged` only branches not "
"merged into the named commit will be listed.  If the <commit> argument is "
"missing it defaults to `HEAD` (i.e. the tip of the current branch)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:62
msgid ""
"The command's second form creates a new branch head named <branchname> which "
"points to the current `HEAD`, or <start-point> if given. As a special case, "
"for <start-point>, you may use `\"A...B\"` as a shortcut for the merge base "
"of `A` and `B` if there is exactly one merge base. You can leave out at most "
"one of `A` and `B`, in which case it defaults to `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:66
msgid ""
"Note that this will create the new branch, but it will not switch the "
"working tree to it; use \"git switch <newbranch>\" to switch to the new "
"branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:74
msgid ""
"When a local branch is started off a remote-tracking branch, Git sets up the "
"branch (specifically the `branch.<name>.remote` and `branch.<name>.merge` "
"configuration entries) so that 'git pull' will appropriately merge from the "
"remote-tracking branch. This behavior may be changed via the global "
"`branch.autoSetupMerge` configuration flag. That setting can be overridden "
"by using the `--track` and `--no-track` options, and changed later using "
"`git branch --set-upstream-to`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:80
msgid ""
"With a `-m` or `-M` option, <oldbranch> will be renamed to <newbranch>.  If "
"<oldbranch> had a corresponding reflog, it is renamed to match <newbranch>, "
"and a reflog entry is created to remember the branch renaming. If "
"<newbranch> exists, -M must be used to force the rename to happen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:84
msgid ""
"The `-c` and `-C` options have the exact same semantics as `-m` and `-M`, "
"except instead of the branch being renamed, it will be copied to a new name, "
"along with its config and reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:88
msgid ""
"With a `-d` or `-D` option, `<branchname>` will be deleted.  You may specify "
"more than one branch for deletion.  If the branch currently has a reflog "
"then the reflog will also be deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:94
msgid ""
"Use `-r` together with `-d` to delete remote-tracking branches. Note, that "
"it only makes sense to delete remote-tracking branches if they no longer "
"exist in the remote repository or if 'git fetch' was configured not to fetch "
"them again. See also the 'prune' subcommand of linkgit:git-remote[1] for a "
"way to clean up all obsolete remote-tracking branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-d`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--delete`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:103
msgid ""
"Delete a branch. The branch must be fully merged in its upstream branch, or "
"in `HEAD` if no upstream was set with `--track` or `--set-upstream-to`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-D`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:106
msgid "Shortcut for `--delete --force`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--create-reflog`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:116
msgid ""
"Create the branch's reflog.  This activates recording of all changes made to "
"the branch ref, enabling use of date based sha1 expressions such as "
"\"<branchname>@\\{yesterday}\".  Note that in non-bare repositories, reflogs "
"are usually enabled by default by the `core.logAllRefUpdates` config "
"option.  The negated form `--no-create-reflog` only overrides an earlier "
"`--create-reflog`, but currently does not negate the setting of "
"`core.logAllRefUpdates`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-f`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--force`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:126
msgid ""
"Reset <branchname> to <start-point>, even if <branchname> exists "
"already. Without `-f`, 'git branch' refuses to change an existing branch.  "
"In combination with `-d` (or `--delete`), allow deleting the branch "
"irrespective of its merged status, or whether it even points to a valid "
"commit. In combination with `-m` (or `--move`), allow renaming the branch "
"even if the new branch name already exists, the same applies for `-c` (or "
"`--copy`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:130
msgid ""
"Note that 'git branch -f <branchname> [<start-point>]', even with '-f', "
"refuses to change an existing branch `<branchname>` that is checked out in "
"another worktree linked to the same repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-m`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--move`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:134
msgid "Move/rename a branch, together with its config and reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-M`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:137
msgid "Shortcut for `--move --force`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-c`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--copy`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:141
msgid "Copy a branch, together with its config and reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-C`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:144
msgid "Shortcut for `--copy --force`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--color[=<when>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:149
msgid ""
"Color branches to highlight current, local, and remote-tracking branches.  "
"The value must be always (the default), never, or auto."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-color`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:154
msgid ""
"Turn off branch colors, even when the configuration file gives the default "
"to color output.  Same as `--color=never`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-i`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ignore-case`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:158
msgid "Sorting and filtering branches are case insensitive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--omit-empty`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:162
msgid ""
"Do not print a newline after formatted refs where the format expands to the "
"empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--column[=<options>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-column`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:168
msgid ""
"Display branch listing in columns. See configuration variable "
"`column.branch` for option syntax. `--column` and `--no-column` without "
"options are equivalent to 'always' and 'never' respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:170
msgid "This option is only applicable in non-verbose mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-r`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--remotes`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:175
msgid ""
"List or delete (if used with -d) the remote-tracking branches.  Combine with "
"`--list` to match the optional pattern(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-a`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--all`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:180
msgid ""
"List both remote-tracking branches and local branches.  Combine with "
"`--list` to match optional pattern(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-l`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--list`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:186
msgid ""
"List branches.  With optional `<pattern>...`, e.g. `git branch --list "
"'maint-*'`, list only the branches that match the pattern(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--show-current`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:190
msgid ""
"Print the name of the current branch. In detached HEAD state, nothing is "
"printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-vv`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:201
msgid ""
"When in list mode, show sha1 and commit subject line for each head, along "
"with relationship to upstream branch (if any). If given twice, print the "
"path of the linked worktree (if any) and the name of the upstream branch, as "
"well (see also `git remote show <remote>`).  Note that the current "
"worktree's HEAD will not have its path printed (it will always be your "
"current directory)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:206
msgid ""
"Be more quiet when creating or deleting a branch, suppressing non-error "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--abbrev=<n>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:213
msgid ""
"In the verbose listing that show the commit object name, show the shortest "
"prefix that is at least '<n>' hexdigits long that uniquely refers the "
"object.  The default value is 7 and can be overridden by the `core.abbrev` "
"config option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-abbrev`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:216
msgid "Display the full sha1s in the output listing rather than abbreviating them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-t`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--track[=(direct|inherit)]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:226
msgid ""
"When creating a new branch, set up `branch.<name>.remote` and "
"`branch.<name>.merge` configuration entries to set \"upstream\" tracking "
"configuration for the new branch. This configuration will tell git to show "
"the relationship between the two branches in `git status` and `git branch "
"-v`. Furthermore, it directs `git pull` without arguments to pull from the "
"upstream when the new branch is checked out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:231
msgid ""
"The exact upstream branch is chosen depending on the optional argument: "
"`-t`, `--track`, or `--track=direct` means to use the start-point branch "
"itself as the upstream; `--track=inherit` means to copy the upstream "
"configuration of the start-point branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:235
msgid ""
"The branch.autoSetupMerge configuration variable specifies how `git switch`, "
"`git checkout` and `git branch` should behave when neither `--track` nor "
"`--no-track` are specified:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:243
msgid ""
"The default option, `true`, behaves as though `--track=direct` were given "
"whenever the start-point is a remote-tracking branch.  `false` behaves as if "
"`--no-track` were given. `always` behaves as though `--track=direct` were "
"given. `inherit` behaves as though `--track=inherit` were given. `simple` "
"behaves as though `--track=direct` were given only when the start-point is a "
"remote-tracking branch and the new branch has the same name as the remote "
"branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:246
msgid ""
"See linkgit:git-pull[1] and linkgit:git-config[1] for additional discussion "
"on how the `branch.<name>.remote` and `branch.<name>.merge` options are "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-track`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:250
msgid ""
"Do not set up \"upstream\" configuration, even if the branch.autoSetupMerge "
"configuration variable is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--recurse-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:257
msgid ""
"THIS OPTION IS EXPERIMENTAL! Causes the current command to recurse into "
"submodules if `submodule.propagateBranches` is enabled. See "
"`submodule.propagateBranches` in linkgit:git-config[1]. Currently, only "
"branch creation is supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:266
msgid ""
"When used in branch creation, a new branch <branchname> will be created in "
"the superproject and all of the submodules in the superproject's "
"<start-point>. In submodules, the branch will point to the submodule commit "
"in the superproject's <start-point> but the branch's tracking information "
"will be set up based on the submodule's branches and remotes e.g. `git "
"branch --recurse-submodules topic origin/main` will create the submodule "
"branch \"topic\" that points to the submodule commit in the superproject's "
"\"origin/main\", but tracks the submodule's \"origin/main\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--set-upstream`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:270
msgid ""
"As this option had confusing syntax, it is no longer supported.  Please use "
"`--track` or `--set-upstream-to` instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-u <upstream>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--set-upstream-to=<upstream>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:276
msgid ""
"Set up <branchname>'s tracking information so <upstream> is considered "
"<branchname>'s upstream branch. If no <branchname> is specified, then it "
"defaults to the current branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--unset-upstream`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:280
msgid ""
"Remove the upstream information for <branchname>. If no branch is specified "
"it defaults to the current branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:281
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--edit-description`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:286
msgid ""
"Open an editor and edit the text to explain what the branch is for, to be "
"used by various other commands (e.g. `format-patch`, `request-pull`, and "
"`merge` (if enabled)). Multi-line explanations may be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--contains [<commit>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:290
msgid ""
"Only list branches which contain the specified commit (HEAD if not "
"specified). Implies `--list`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:291
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-contains [<commit>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:294
msgid ""
"Only list branches which don't contain the specified commit (HEAD if not "
"specified). Implies `--list`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:295
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--merged [<commit>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:298
msgid ""
"Only list branches whose tips are reachable from the specified commit (HEAD "
"if not specified). Implies `--list`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-merged [<commit>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:302
msgid ""
"Only list branches whose tips are not reachable from the specified commit "
"(HEAD if not specified). Implies `--list`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "<branchname>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:308
msgid ""
"The name of the branch to create or delete.  The new branch name must pass "
"all checks defined by linkgit:git-check-ref-format[1].  Some of these checks "
"may restrict the characters allowed in a branch name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "<start-point>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:313
msgid ""
"The new branch head will point to this commit.  It may be given as a branch "
"name, a commit-id, or a tag.  If this option is omitted, the current HEAD "
"will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:314
#, no-wrap
msgid "<oldbranch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:317
msgid ""
"The name of an existing branch.  If this option is omitted, the name of the "
"current branch will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:318
#, no-wrap
msgid "<newbranch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:321
msgid ""
"The new name for an existing branch. The same restrictions as for "
"<branchname> apply."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--sort=<key>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:332
msgid ""
"Sort based on the key given. Prefix `-` to sort in descending order of the "
"value. You may use the --sort=<key> option multiple times, in which case the "
"last key becomes the primary key. The keys supported are the same as those "
"in `git for-each-ref`. Sort order defaults to the value configured for the "
"`branch.sort` variable if it exists, or to sorting based on the full refname "
"(including `refs/...` prefix). This lists detached HEAD (if present) first, "
"then local branches and finally remote-tracking branches. See "
"linkgit:git-config[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--points-at <object>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:336
msgid "Only list branches of the given object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:337
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--format <format>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:341
msgid ""
"A string that interpolates `%(fieldname)` from a branch ref being shown and "
"the object it points at.  The format is the same as that of "
"linkgit:git-for-each-ref[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:347
msgid ""
"`pager.branch` is only respected when listing branches, i.e., when `--list` "
"is used or implied. The default is to use a pager.  See "
"linkgit:git-config[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:353
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:355
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start development from a known tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git clone git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/.../linux-2.6 my2.6\n"
"$ cd my2.6\n"
"$ git branch my2.6.14 v2.6.14   <1>\n"
"$ git switch my2.6.14\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:366
msgid ""
"This step and the next one could be combined into a single step with "
"\"checkout -b my2.6.14 v2.6.14\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:367
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete an unneeded branch"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:374
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git clone git://git.kernel.org/.../git.git my.git\n"
"$ cd my.git\n"
"$ git branch -d -r origin/todo origin/html origin/man   <1>\n"
"$ git branch -D test                                    <2>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:379
msgid ""
"Delete the remote-tracking branches \"todo\", \"html\" and \"man\". The next "
"'fetch' or 'pull' will create them again unless you configure them not to.  "
"See linkgit:git-fetch[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:381
msgid ""
"Delete the \"test\" branch even if the \"master\" branch (or whichever "
"branch is currently checked out) does not have all commits from the test "
"branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:382
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listing branches from a specific remote"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:387
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git branch -r -l '<remote>/<pattern>'                 <1>\n"
"$ git for-each-ref 'refs/remotes/<remote>/<pattern>'    <2>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:391
msgid ""
"Using `-a` would conflate <remote> with any local branches you happen to "
"have been prefixed with the same <remote> pattern."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:392
msgid ""
"`for-each-ref` can take a wide range of options. See "
"linkgit:git-for-each-ref[1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:394
msgid "Patterns will normally need quoting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:396
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:401
msgid ""
"If you are creating a branch that you want to switch to immediately, it is "
"easier to use the \"git switch\" command with its `-c` option to do the same "
"thing with a single command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:404
msgid ""
"The options `--contains`, `--no-contains`, `--merged` and `--no-merged` "
"serve four related but different purposes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:408
msgid ""
"`--contains <commit>` is used to find all branches which will need special "
"attention if <commit> were to be rebased or amended, since those branches "
"contain the specified <commit>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:411
msgid ""
"`--no-contains <commit>` is the inverse of that, i.e. branches that don't "
"contain the specified <commit>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:414
msgid ""
"`--merged` is used to find all branches which can be safely deleted, since "
"those branches are fully contained by HEAD."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-branch.txt:417
msgid ""
"`--no-merged` is used to find branches which are candidates for merging into "
"HEAD, since those branches are not fully contained by HEAD."
msgstr ""

